<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Mukish</h1><p class="st-meta">2000 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.) · capital Alalakh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Mukish, the kingdom of Alalakh in the Amuq plain, best known for King Idrimi, whose statue tells the story of an exiled prince who won back a throne.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alalakh">Alalakh</a>, at Tell Atchana near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antakya</a>, was a town of the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amuq-valley">Amuq plain</a> by the early 2nd millennium BCE. In the 18th century BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abba-el-i">Abba-El</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yamhad">Yamhad</a> granted it to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yarim-lim-of-alalakh">Yarim-Lim</a>, making it a dependent kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonard-woolley">Leonard Woolley's</a> excavations from 1937 recovered palaces and archives from this period.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alalakh">Alalakh's</a> palace archives record a society of nobles who owned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a>, free farmers and dependent labourers, written in Akkadian with many Hurrian names. After a Hittite destruction c. 1600 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idrimi">Idrimi</a>, a refugee prince from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, took the city and ruled Mukish as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mitanni-empire">Mitanni Empire</a>, as his inscribed statue relates.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> conquered Mukish in the 14th century BCE and gave some of its land to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ugarit">Ugarit</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alalakh">Alalakh</a> was abandoned around 1200 BCE, during the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a>, and its region later formed part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/patina">Patina</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 2000 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:19.90%;width:15.92%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2000 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Alalakh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yarim-Lim, Idrimi, Niqmepa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hurrian and Syrian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian, Hurrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alalakh, Mukish</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mukish" aria-label="Kingdom of Mukish on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5596 870 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Mukish lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5916 1126L5935 1127M5916 1126L5996 1079M5916 1126L5852 1002"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5935 1127h0M5996 1079h0M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5916 1126h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5916 1126h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Alalakh. <a href="/atlas?year=-1600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-mukish">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

